{"amendments":[{"body":"crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:229-239 now emits `nitrogen_cycle.total_n_nitrified_mg` beside `nitrogen_cycle.alk_consumed_meq`, but those two notes are not measuring the same nitrogen flow. `total_mg_n_nitrified` is computed as `nob_step.oxidized_n_mg + comammox_step.oxidized_n_mg` in crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:343-346, while alkalinity consumption is driven by `aob_alk_cost + comammox_alk_cost` in crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:366-384. In ticks where AOB produces nitrite that NOB does not finish oxidizing, the trace will under-report the N associated with the alkalinity loss and the two diagnostics become internally inconsistent. Trace the TAN-oxidation amount instead, or rename the nitrate-only metric so it cannot be mistaken for the alkalinity-coupled quantity.","rationale":"These changes are specifically about diagnostics. A trace that presents two related numbers that disagree in normal nitrite-accumulation cases will mislead anyone trying to debug a conservation failure."},{"body":"crates/tank_core/src/budget_helpers.rs:442-477 and crates/tank_core/src/budget_helpers.rs:494-507 still format alkalinity failures as `mg` even when `element == Element::Alkalinity`, even though the underlying budget is explicitly `meq` in crates/tank_core/src/types/budget.rs:72-76 and crates/tank_core/src/types/budget.rs:106-109. That means a failing alkalinity assertion will report the wrong units for the net delta, per-stage deltas, and tolerance, which makes the new diagnostics easy to misread and encourages callers to treat a meq check like an mg check. Add an alkalinity-aware formatting/helper path instead of reusing the mg-oriented output.","rationale":"The budget helpers are the first thing engineers see when a regression trips. If the failure text labels alkalinity as mg, the new diagnostic surface is materially misleading rather than merely cosmetic."}],"summary":"Reviewed the nested worktree patch and ran targeted tank_core tests (`--test nitrification_alkalinity`, `--test water_change_mass_balance`, `--test budget_helpers`). I found two diagnostics issues: one misleading new nitrogen-cycle trace metric, and one unit-reporting bug in the new alkalinity budget helpers."}